      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "data_vm\n\nThe kernel explicitly added this to track a process's private writable data space. Notice the logic gates: it\nmust be writable (VM_WRITE), but it cannot be a shared mapping (~VM_SHARED), and it cannot be the stack\n(~VM_STACK).\n\nThe kernel needs this field because of RLIMIT_DATA (the maximum size of a process's data segment). Every\ntime a process calls brk() or allocates anonymous private memory, the kernel verifies it against data_vm to\nensure the process isn't blowing past its system-enforced memory limits.",
      "fontSize": 34.6528980602038,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "data_vm\n\nThe kernel explicitly added this to track a process's private writable data space. Notice the logic gates: it must be writable (VM_WRITE), but it cannot be a shared mapping (~VM_SHARED), and it cannot be the stack (~VM_STACK).\n\nThe kernel needs this field because of RLIMIT_DATA (the maximum size of a process's data segment). Every time a process calls brk() or allocates anonymous private memory, the kernel verifies it against data_vm to ensure the process isn't blowing past its system-enforced memory limits.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
