      ],
      "updated": 1784407572480,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "fd_array\n\nfd_array: This is a static array of pointers to struct file objects. \nOn standard x86 architectures, NR_OPEN_DEFAULT is typically set to 32 or 64.\n\nBecause it's embedded right inside the structure, the pointers for standard descriptors—like 0 (stdin), 1 (stdout), 2 (stderr), \nand your initial opened files—are allocated in a single contiguous block of memory. The CPU can fetch these pointers incredibly fast without chasing heap pointers.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "fd_array\n\nfd_array: This is a static array of pointers to struct file objects. \nOn standard x86 architectures, NR_OPEN_DEFAULT is typically set to 32 or 64.\n\nBecause it's embedded right inside the structure, the pointers for standard descriptors—like 0 (stdin), 1 (stdout), 2 (stderr), \nand your initial opened files—are allocated in a single contiguous block of memory. The CPU can fetch these pointers incredibly fast without chasing heap pointers.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
