    {
      "id": "UhQ9X0-c8Rqt9HRCZZB2o",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -7001.586472382279,
      "y": -468.6685121521009,
      "width": 1384.13330078125,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1216295313,
      "version": 37,
      "versionNonce": 377294559,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "saflfc0ZlX37XaXn1csvt",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1784443852701,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "rcu\n\nWhen the table resizes, the kernel allocates a new fdtable and instantly \nchanges the process's tracking pointer to look at the new one. However, \nother CPU cores might still be looking up a file in the old table at that \nexact microsecond. The rcu_head is a tiny structure that tells the kernel: \n\"Don't free this memory immediately. Wait until all active readers finish looking \nup their files, then safely destroy this old table in the background.\"",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "rcu\n\nWhen the table resizes, the kernel allocates a new fdtable and instantly \nchanges the process's tracking pointer to look at the new one. However, \nother CPU cores might still be looking up a file in the old table at that \nexact microsecond. The rcu_head is a tiny structure that tells the kernel: \n\"Don't free this memory immediately. Wait until all active readers finish looking \nup their files, then safely destroy this old table in the background.\"",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": null,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
